IMPORT prelude
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §2.6 card B1 (RULED 2026-09-21, built in part
-- 2026-10-24): THE JOIN, THE DEADLINE and THE ARMING are VALUES — NUMBERs on
-- the trace's clock — wherever an expression goes, not only after OF.
--
-- What a noun names is the instant that position had in the life of the
-- obligation whose HENCE or LEST the noun is WRITTEN in (THE ARMING at the
-- top level: the obligation's own arming) — with one exception. Inside an
-- obligation that is handed on as a VALUE (a WHERE local, a GIVEN, a
-- function's result), a noun is read where that obligation RUNS, under the
-- obligation it is attached to, as its anchors are: obligation values are
-- re-anchored at hand-off, NUMBER aliases are fixed where they are written
-- (dossier B1, EVERY-EACH-ANCHOR-SLOT-BENCH-2026-09-15.md). §3 is the
-- NUMBER alias; §12 is the obligation value, and shows that moving the same
-- expression between the two moves the deadline. The refusals are the
-- anchor's (run-anchors.l4); not-ok/tc/lifecycle-value-*.l4 pins them.
--
-- Every trace pins one value to a number, and the number a breach reports
-- is the deadline that value produced.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Deliver HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Refund  HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Pay     HAS amount IS A NUMBER

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
bob         MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"
tenants     MEANS LIST alice, bob


§ `1. arithmetic on THE JOIN`

-- Alice signs at 8; the landlord must deliver by THE JOIN PLUS 5 = 13. The
-- anchor is an expression, so the WITHIN counts zero days from it. Written
-- bare after OF, with the arithmetic on the same line, it is the same
-- expression (the second rule): delivery at 13 is timely, at 14 the breach
-- reports 13.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`join plus five` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord WITHIN 0 OF (THE JOIN PLUS 5))
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `join plus five` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 13

#TRACE `join plus five` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 14

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`join plus five, unbracketed` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord WITHIN 0 OF THE JOIN PLUS 5)
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `join plus five, unbracketed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 14

-- The operator may start the next line, indented as a continuation: the
-- same expression, the same 13. (Until the review of 2026-10-24 only the
-- noun's own line counted, and this was an ambiguity about __PLUS__.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`join plus five, operator on the next line` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord WITHIN 0 OF THE JOIN
             PLUS 5)
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `join plus five, operator on the next line` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 14


§ `2. a continuation defined elsewhere receives the instant by argument`

-- B1's ruling: a continuation handed on as a value receives an outer
-- position by ARGUMENT. `refund within 30 of` is a top-level rule, where
-- THE JOIN names nothing; the HENCE passes it the join it means, Alice's
-- signature at 4, so the landlord's deadline is 4 + 30 = 34. The second
-- rule passes it by name (WITH … IS THE JOIN), which is the same call.
GIVEN start IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`refund within 30 of` MEANS
    PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 30 OF start

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`passed by argument` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE `refund within 30 of` THE JOIN

#TRACE `passed by argument` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 34

#TRACE `passed by argument` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 35

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`passed by name` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE `refund within 30 of` WITH start IS THE JOIN

#TRACE `passed by name` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 35


§ `3. a WHERE alias keeps the instant it was written under`

-- "Acknowledge within 5, and resolve within 30 of RECEIPT." Receipt is
-- Alice's signature, at 8. The alias `receipt` is written in the HENCE of
-- her obligation, so it is THAT join, and it keeps it when the refund
-- obligation is two hand-offs down: the refund falls due at 8 + 30 = 38,
-- not at 10 + 30 = 40 (the acknowledgement's join, which a bare THE JOIN
-- in the refund's WITHIN would name). Refund at 38 is timely; at 39 the
-- breach reports 38.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`resolve within 30 of receipt` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (    PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord WITHIN 5
               HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 30 OF receipt)
           WHERE receipt MEANS THE JOIN)

#TRACE `resolve within 30 of receipt` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 10
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 38

#TRACE `resolve within 30 of receipt` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 10
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 39


§ `4. a default for an anchor that may be missing (card B4)`

-- The slot takes an instant, never a MAYBE (B4, frozen): a fact that may
-- not have been recorded gets its default from the drafter, here THE
-- ARMING — the arming of the obligation this one continues, Alice's, at 0.
-- No notice was ever recorded, so the landlord's five days run from 0.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`five days of notice, or of the arming` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord WITHIN 5 OF (fromMaybe THE ARMING (RECALL `notice served`)))

#TRACE `five days of notice, or of the arming` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 5

#TRACE `five days of notice, or of the arming` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 6


§ `5. THE DEADLINE under LEST, plus a grace period`

-- Alice misses day 10; the cure runs to THE DEADLINE PLUS 5 = 15, whatever
-- day the miss came to light (her signature at 14 is re-offered to the LEST
-- and discharges it; at 16 the breach reports 15).
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`cure to the deadline plus five` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 0 OF (THE DEADLINE PLUS 5))

#TRACE `cure to the deadline plus five` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 14

#TRACE `cure to the deadline plus five` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 16


§ `6. a barrier's HENCE reads the group's join`

-- Both tenants sign (the last at 7), the group's join fires at 7, and the
-- landlord's deadline is THE JOIN PLUS 3 = 10.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`after everyone signs` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN 20
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord WITHIN 0 OF (THE JOIN PLUS 3))

#TRACE `after everyone signs` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 2
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 7
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 11


§ `7. THE JOIN in the NEXT obligation's PROVIDED is the PREVIOUS act's time`

-- Lexical, so read with care: in Bob's PROVIDED, which is written in the
-- HENCE of Alice's obligation, THE JOIN is Alice's signature (at 6) — not
-- the time of the payment being tested. Bob must pay an amount of at least
-- that number: 6 is accepted; 5 is not his act, so his obligation is
-- still waiting when the trace ends (the residual prints THE JOIN as
-- written).
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`pay at least the join` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE (PARTY bob MUST Pay n PROVIDED n AT LEAST THE JOIN WITHIN 10)

#TRACE `pay at least the join` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 6
  PARTY bob   DOES Pay 6 AT 9

#TRACE `pay at least the join` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 6
  PARTY bob   DOES Pay 5 AT 9


§ `8. RECORD a lifecycle value, RECALL it later`

-- The ledger stores the number, so a fact recorded at the join can anchor a
-- deadline much later: the join is at 4, the landlord's 30 days run to 34.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`record the receipt` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE RECORD `receipt` IS THE JOIN
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 30 OF (fromMaybe 0 (RECALL `receipt`)))

#TRACE `record the receipt` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 35


§ `9. THE ARMING at the top level is the obligation's own arming`

-- With no enclosing obligation THE ARMING is the obligation's own arming,
-- whether written bare after OF, as a value alone in the slot, or as a
-- value in arithmetic: all three deadlines are 10 + 5, so a signature at
-- 15 is in time and one at 16 is a breach reporting 15.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`own arming, as a value` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 0 OF (THE ARMING PLUS 5)

#TRACE `own arming, as a value` AT 10 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 15

#TRACE `own arming, as a value` AT 10 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 16

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`own arming, bare` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 5 OF THE ARMING

#TRACE `own arming, bare` AT 10 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 16

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`own arming, alone in brackets` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 5 OF (THE ARMING)

#TRACE `own arming, alone in brackets` AT 10 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 15

#TRACE `own arming, alone in brackets` AT 10 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 16

-- Bare after OF with the arithmetic on the same line, as in §1: one
-- expression, so the deadline is 10 + 3 = 13 and a signature at 13 is in
-- time, at 14 a breach reporting 13.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`own arming plus three, unbracketed` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 0 OF THE ARMING PLUS 3

#TRACE `own arming plus three, unbracketed` AT 10 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 13

#TRACE `own arming plus three, unbracketed` AT 10 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 14


§ `10. on a join line, THE ARMING is the EVERY's own arming however deep it sits`

-- The EVERY is armed when the landlord delivers, at 5. On its join line
-- THE ARMING means that arming, as a bare OF THE ARMING there does (not the
-- landlord's, at 0): the group must finish by 5 + 10 = 15. Bob's signature
-- at 15 is in time; at 16 the group misses its deadline of 15.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`join line of the arming, nested` MEANS
    PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord WITHIN 10
    HENCE (EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
               MUST   Sign t
               WITHIN 20
               ONCE   ALL HAVE
               WITHIN 0 OF (THE ARMING PLUS 10))

#TRACE `join line of the arming, nested` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 5
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 6
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 15

#TRACE `join line of the arming, nested` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 5
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 6
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 16

-- That is the noun written ON the join line. A WHERE name for the same
-- expression, written in the landlord's HENCE, is a NUMBER fixed there,
-- where THE ARMING is the landlord's own, at 0: the group must finish by
-- 0 + 10 = 10, and Bob's signature at 15 misses it.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`join line of an alias, nested` MEANS
    PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord WITHIN 10
    HENCE (EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
               MUST   Sign t
               WITHIN 20
               ONCE   ALL HAVE
               WITHIN 0 OF w
           WHERE w MEANS THE ARMING PLUS 10)

#TRACE `join line of an alias, nested` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 5
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 6
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 15


§ `11. a top-level WHERE reaches no obligation (moved)`

-- This section ran `WHERE t MEANS THE ARMING` on a top-level rule and
-- pinned the run's refusal. The checker now refuses it where it is written
-- (refusal 8, card B1c), so it lives in
-- not-ok/tc/lifecycle-arming-outside-obligation.l4. The number is kept so
-- that citations of the sections after it stay right.


§ `12. inside an obligation handed on as a value, a noun is read where it runs`

-- Alice signs at 4 and the landlord delivers at 10. `k` is an OBLIGATION
-- defined in the WHERE of Alice's HENCE and attached under the landlord's
-- HENCE, so it runs there: its THE JOIN is the delivery, at 10, the same
-- as an anchor in it would be, and the refund is due at 10 + 5 = 15 (a
-- refund at 16 reports 15).
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`a value inside a handed-on obligation` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (    PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord WITHIN 30
               HENCE k
           WHERE k MEANS PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 0 OF (THE JOIN PLUS 5))

#TRACE `a value inside a handed-on obligation` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 10
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 16

-- The same deadline written through a WHERE name inside `k`'s definition:
-- `t` is a NUMBER, fixed where `k` is defined, in Alice's HENCE, where THE
-- JOIN is her signature at 4. So the refund is due at 4 + 5 = 9, before
-- `k` is even entered at 10, and it fails there. Moving the expression
-- into a WHERE moved the deadline from 15 to 9, and nothing said so but
-- the run's note.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`a WHERE name inside a handed-on obligation` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (    PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord WITHIN 30
               HENCE k
           WHERE k MEANS PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 0 OF t
                     WHERE t MEANS THE JOIN PLUS 5)

#TRACE `a WHERE name inside a handed-on obligation` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 10
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 16

-- A PROVIDED inside `k` reads the same way: n EQUALS THE JOIN is tested
-- against the delivery's 10, not Alice's 4 where it is written. A payment
-- of 4 does not match and the obligation stays open; a payment of 10 is
-- FULFILLED.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`a PROVIDED inside a handed-on obligation` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (    PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord WITHIN 30
               HENCE k
           WHERE k MEANS PARTY bob MUST Pay n PROVIDED n EQUALS THE JOIN WITHIN 50)

#TRACE `a PROVIDED inside a handed-on obligation` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 10
  PARTY bob DOES Pay 4 AT 12

#TRACE `a PROVIDED inside a handed-on obligation` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 10
  PARTY bob DOES Pay 10 AT 12


§ `13. THE ARMING in an EVERY's roll and filter, and on a top-level EVERY's own lines`

-- An EVERY's IN roll and its WHO filter are read where the EVERY is
-- written, before any member is armed, so under a HENCE THE ARMING there is
-- the arming of the obligation whose HENCE holds the EVERY: the landlord's,
-- entered when Alice signs. (At the top level the same roll and filter are
-- refused: not-ok/tc/lifecycle-arming-in-every-roll.l4.) Here the roll is
-- Alice alone when the landlord's obligation was entered after day 10, and
-- both tenants otherwise. The group then countersigns within 10 of the
-- delivery at 13. Alice signs at 12, so only she is called, and her
-- countersignature at 14 completes the group; signing at 4 calls Bob as
-- well, and he misses 13 + 10 = 23.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF Actor
`tenants from` MEANS IF n GREATER THAN 10 THEN LIST alice ELSE tenants

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`a roll read from the arming` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord WITHIN 30
           HENCE (EVERY Tenant t IN (`tenants from` THE ARMING)
                      MUST   Sign t
                      WITHIN 10
                      ONCE   ALL HAVE
                      HENCE  FULFILLED))

#TRACE `a roll read from the arming` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 12
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 13
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 14
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

#TRACE `a roll read from the arming` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 13
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 14
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

-- The same choice made by a WHO filter over both tenants: the same answers.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`a filter read from the arming` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord WITHIN 30
           HENCE (EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
                      WHO    (t EQUALS alice) OR (THE ARMING AT MOST 10)
                      MUST   Sign t
                      WITHIN 10
                      ONCE   ALL HAVE
                      HENCE  FULFILLED))

#TRACE `a filter read from the arming` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 12
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 13
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 14
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

#TRACE `a filter read from the arming` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 13
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 14
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

-- On a top-level EVERY's act line and join line, THE ARMING is the EVERY's
-- own arming, here 5. On the act line: each tenant must sign by 5 + 10 =
-- 15, and Bob's signature at 16 is a breach reporting 15. On the join line:
-- with each tenant given to 5 + 20 = 25, the group must be complete by
-- 5 + 10 = 15, so Bob's signature at 15 is in time and at 16 the group
-- misses 15, though his own deadline is still open.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`act line of a top-level group` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN 0 OF (THE ARMING PLUS 10)

#TRACE `act line of a top-level group` AT 5 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 16

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`own lines of a top-level group` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN 0 OF (THE ARMING PLUS 20)
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        WITHIN 0 OF (THE ARMING PLUS 10)
        HENCE  FULFILLED

#TRACE `own lines of a top-level group` AT 5 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 15

#TRACE `own lines of a top-level group` AT 5 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 16


§ `14. THE JOIN under a SHANT's LEST is the act that broke it`

-- Under a prohibition's LEST, THE JOIN is the stamp of the violating act
-- (breach-clocks.l4 §9 writes it as an anchor), and it is a value there
-- like anywhere else. Bob may not sign in the first 10 days; he signs at 3,
-- so the refund is due at THE JOIN PLUS 2 = 5. A refund at 5 discharges
-- it; at 6 the breach reports 5.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`a broken prohibition, cured by a value` MEANS
    PARTY bob SHANT Sign bob WITHIN 10
    LEST  (PARTY bob MUST Refund bob WITHIN 0 OF (THE JOIN PLUS 2))

#TRACE `a broken prohibition, cured by a value` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY bob DOES Sign bob AT 3
  PARTY bob DOES Refund bob AT 5

#TRACE `a broken prohibition, cured by a value` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY bob DOES Sign bob AT 3
  PARTY bob DOES Refund bob AT 6


§ `15. a lifecycle value opens an AFTER window`

-- AFTER takes the nouns as values too: AFTER 0 OF (THE JOIN PLUS 3) opens
-- at the same instant as AFTER 3 OF THE JOIN (doc/reference/regulative/AFTER.md).
-- Alice signs at 4, so the delivery window opens at 7 and, with the WITHIN
-- bare, stays open 10 after that, to 17. A delivery at 6 is early, a
-- nullity the run notes; one at 7 is in time. With no delivery after the
-- early one, the breach reports 17. Both spellings give both answers.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`a window opened by a value` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord AFTER 0 OF (THE JOIN PLUS 3) WITHIN 10)

#TRACE `a window opened by a value` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 6
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 7

#TRACE `a window opened by a value` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 6
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`a window opened by the anchor` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord AFTER 3 OF THE JOIN WITHIN 10)

#TRACE `a window opened by the anchor` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 6
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 7

#TRACE `a window opened by the anchor` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 6
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)
